  "source": {
    "url": "https://assets-cdn.liebherr.com/versions/06b44b8e-873d-4805-b9c4-3ea285217eb6/original/",
    "title": "Liebherr Technical data - Mobile crane LTM 1090-4.2 [m/t] (liebherr-271-ltm-1090-4.2-td-271-06-defisr11-2023, linked from liebherr.com product page)",
    "page": "13 (load chart maxt_271_001_00001_00/ 00301_00 / 00341_00); dimensions p.3",
    "retrieved": "2026-09-24"
  },
  "notes": "Values from the official Liebherr metric datasheet (p.13: 360°, 22.5 t, VarioBallast). The table is a combined VarioBallast chart: light cells are valid at 3.77 m ballast radius, dark cells need 4.71 m; all values are valid at 4.71 m, which is what this file assumes (tailSwingRadius 4.71 m; 3.77 m when retracted, both R shown on the top view). 16 boom lengths in source; 33.8, 44.9, 55.6 and 59.4 m omitted to keep 12 columns. 11.4 m boom has an over-rear (±0°) '*' sub-column (90 t at 3 m = headline rating) which is NOT stored. Outrigger span not printed on the table; longitudinal 7.474 m (lower chain; upper 7.446 m), transverse 7.3 m max (VarioBase 2.32-7.3 m). Max supporting force 533 kN (55 t), p.9. Operating weight not stated: jobsite ≤ 64 t with 22.5 t counterweight; on-road ≤ 48 t (4 x 12 t) with 7.4/8.8 t (p.10). maxHookHeight not taken (graph only). Overall length incl. superstructure 13.390 m. Dims from the side/top dimension drawing: overallLength_m = carrier length (bottom dimension chain, carrier front to rear); axle positions and slew centre are cumulative sums of that chain, measured from the carrier front. Height/width = columns A/B-or-C of the dimension table for the standard 385/95 R 25 (14.00 R 25) tyres. wheelDiameter_m is NOT from the drawing: nominal value computed from the tyre designation (25 in rim + 2 x 95% x 385 mm = 1.37 m). Boom pivot height/offset are not dimensioned on the drawing (null). Liebherr remarks: hook block weight is part of the load (chartIncludesHookBlock true). Dimension reference corrected: the datasheet's bottom dimension chain starts at the front of the boom head (transport position, boom overhanging the cab), not at the carrier front bumper. overallLength_m is now the carrier length (front bumper to rear) and axlePositions_m / slewCentreFromFront_m are measured from the carrier front bumper; the boom head overhang ahead of the bumper is stored as boomOverhangFront_m = 1.539 m (overall transport length incl. boom = 13.09 m). Evidence (dimensions drawing p.3): chain 1539 | 11551 = 13090, carrier chain 2241 | 2480 | 2860 | 1670 | 2300 = 11551; slew centre 500 behind 3rd axle."
